Note: Symbol literal interning + strict separation from String (SYM-01)
Note: Tests: pointer-equality on same intern slot, (equals Symbol Symbol) true, (equals Symbol String) false
Note: Phase 26.1 Wave 1 — see plan 26.1-02 / CONTEXT § Specifics block 1

use "@std"

Note: ===== Test 1: Symbol literal lexes + evaluates =====
Symbol kick = #kick
(print (str kick))

Note: ===== Test 2: Same-name interning gives pointer equality via (equals) =====
Symbol kickAgain = #kick
Bool sameKick = (equals kick kickAgain)
(print (str sameKick))

Note: ===== Test 3: Different names compare unequal =====
Symbol snare = #snare
Bool diffSym = (equals kick snare)
(print (str diffSym))

Note: ===== Test 4: Strict separation from String =====
String kickStr = "kick"
Bool symVsStr = (equals kick kickStr)
(print (str symVsStr))

Note: ===== Test 5: Two distinct symbols still distinct via (equals) =====
Bool snareVsKick = (equals snare #kick)
(print (str snareVsKick))

(print "test_symbol_literal: PASSED")
